From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:15:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 53/64] fix(registry): re-pin gauntlet-tdd 0.1.0 to the
 post-fix pack subtree (gcp-dnxq)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 0.1.0 release was stamped against c84a27b, the commit that introduced the
pack. 420f8da then changed the pack subtree — the lint-flag, JSON-stream and
cross-step-state fixes — so the pin still validated (the hash is recomputed at
the named commit, and that commit's tree is unchanged) while naming a version
of the pack with three known defects in it. A release that validates and ships
the wrong bytes is worse than one that fails: nothing surfaces.

Re-pinned to 420f8da with the hash recomputed by validate_registry.py's own
`git_pack_content_hash` over the pack subtree at that commit, so the published
0.1.0 is the content that was actually tested.

`python3 validate_registry.py --require-git` -> `registry.toml: ok`.
---
 registry.toml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/registry.toml b/registry.toml
index 255dfc7..e715e73 100644
--- a/registry.toml
+++ b/registry.toml
@@ -323,6 +323,6 @@ schema = 1
   [[pack.release]]
     version = "0.1.0"
     ref = "main"
-    commit = "c84a27ba9bc290f67cbf24ba86e663e7268d6798"
-    hash = "sha256:3e93803831adc79d19da3d9bb06e9bc23518d1013ab1432da81a4d18b40de7ff"
+    commit = "420f8daaf01ba785f57d84c60350583774c9860f"
+    hash = "sha256:98335fdb161766ec56b897e05a2b576677714d3defe402f9d696528871f62a6d"
     description = "Initial gauntlet-tdd release: the RED-to-GREEN contract loop as one formula (mol-tdd-red-green) plus a wrapper command, pinned to the bats lane with gauntlet lint as the red gate."
